      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-5539",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Using the formula for the distance, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(x,y) & =\u2016x-y\u2016 \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{y}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{y}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{y}_{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1-2)^{2}+(2-0)^{2}+(3-(-1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+4+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/example-5539.json",
